# Runtime state, never committed.
#
# suppression-list.json holds real opted-out addresses (personal data) and
# send-audit.log holds the same addresses in dispatch records. Both are
# regenerated at runtime and are shared between the opt-out origin and the send
# preflight by being one file behind one origin (resolveStorePath()), not by
# being in version control.
#
# A fresh clone therefore has no store — and the preflight fails closed (exit
# code 3) rather than reporting a clear list. That is the intended behaviour.
suppression-list.json
send-audit.log
*.tmp
